  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Utah has $162M in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. The federal government awarded 509 contracts in Utah so far, with an average award size of $318K. Obligations are down 97.7% year over year. Fiscal-year totals before FY2027 show previous statewide obligations of $5.3B in FY22, $6.4B in FY23, $7.3B in FY24, $5.3B in FY25, and $7.1B in FY26. The Department of the Treasury and the Department of Veterans Affairs are the top buyers in FY2027 to date, obligating $46.8M and $43M respectively. ASAHI REFINING USA INC and ALPINE COMPANIES, INC. are the top vendors in FY2027 to date, with $42.9M and $27.2M in obligations. Nonferrous Metal (except Copper and Aluminum) Rolling, Drawing, and Extruding and Residential Property Managers are the largest industry recipients in FY2027 to date, with $42.9M and $27.2M respectively. All figures are contract obligations; current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date shows $162M in obligations compared with $7.1B in FY26. Obligations are down 97.7% year over year. FY22 through FY26 obligations were $5.3B, $6.4B, $7.3B, $5.3B, and $7.1B respectively, so FY2027 to date is a smaller partial-year total than any full prior year listed."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries are driving FY2027 to date spending?",
        "body": "The Department of the Treasury and the Department of Veterans Affairs are the top buying agencies with $46.8M and $43M in obligations. ASAHI REFINING USA INC and ALPINE COMPANIES, INC. are the top vendors with $42.9M and $27.2M in obligations. Nonferrous Metal (except Copper and Aluminum) Rolling, Drawing, and Extruding and Residential Property Managers are the top industries with $42.9M and $27.2M in obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
