    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Utah?",
      "a": "Utah received $162M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The federal government awarded 509 contracts in Utah so far, with an average award size of $318K. Obligations are down 97.7% year over year, and prior full-year obligations were $5.3B in FY22, $6.4B in FY23, $7.3B in FY24, $5.3B in FY25, and $7.1B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Utah?",
      "a": "The Department of the Treasury and the Department of Veterans Affairs award the most contracts in Utah in FY2027 to date. The Department of the Treasury obligated $46.8M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $43M. Other top buying agencies include the Department of Housing and Urban Development with $27.2M and the General Services Administration with $14.8M."
